WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.149
Many of us are already accustomed to different ways of proving who we are and we do it.

2
00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:15.539
Perhaps without even knowing it,

3
00:00:16.479 --> 00:00:16.959
usually,

4
00:00:16.969 --> 00:00:19.940
we are asked to authenticate our identities by using something

5
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.569
that we know such as a password or pass phrase.

6
00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:25.360
This is one factor of authentication.

7
00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:29.799
Then we use something that only we have such as a token or card

8
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.680
that gives us two different factors of authentication.

9
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.819
When you go to the bank and use your ATM card,

10
00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:42.299
you may have a user name and password or a specific code such as API

11
00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:45.869
you have the card and you know the pin.

12
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.180
So that is one form of multi factor authentication.

13
00:00:49.529 --> 00:00:52.340
Someone with just the card cannot access the money.

14
00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.240
Then

15
00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:01.770
increasingly we also provide something that we are with biometrics.

16
00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:06.080
This can be a fingerprint or another type of measurable characteristic

17
00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.959
such as facial recognition or an iris scan.

18
00:01:09.449 --> 00:01:13.440
We see these elements of the authentication process on a daily basis.

19
00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.239
This adds another layer of multi factor authentication.